# suspend_gap_restored_fault_at_read: A blob whose root FIFO is enabled with read 0x18, written 0x30 and fault offset (key 19) 0x18: rvg_device_did_resume recreates the FIFO with those counts, 0x103c reads 0x18 and 0x102c 1, but the fault is only a register: the queue is fresh, so the two NOPs between read and written (stamps 7 and 8) run and publish while 0x102c still reads 1. 0x1024 clears it ("Stamp at head isn't faulted"), and the next NOP runs. A fault offset of 0, the register a crafted blob leaves unset, restores the same fault at offset 0: only 0xffffffff means no fault.
